Surgical mechanism to sidestep out of memory problem.  As we load models, we build a model cache which enables models to be recalled on reuse.   A real solution involves much more complication.  See [issue](https://github.com/positron-ai/tron/issues/2101). 

gen/t_generate_host_2 2>&1 | grep Cleared
[2026-02-23 19:46:03.721] [info] Cleared 2 cached model(s), RSS 60.2 GB -> 4.3 GB (freed 55.8 GB)
bill@andoria-15:~/brm$ git diff
diff --git a/src/tron/models/cache.cpp b/src/tron/models/cache.cpp
index a11e9b464..b3e532292 100644
--- a/src/tron/models/cache.cpp
+++ b/src/tron/models/cache.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+#include <fstream>
+#include <string>
+#include <unistd.h>
+
+#include <spdlog/spdlog.h>
+
 #include "tron/models/cache.hpp"
 
 namespace tron {
@@ -12,9 +18,26 @@ std::mutex& model_cache_mutex() {
   return mutex;
 }
 
+// Read current process RSS in bytes from /proc/self/statm.
+static size_t get_rss_bytes() {
+  std::ifstream statm("/proc/self/statm");
+  size_t pages_total, pages_rss;
+  if (statm >> pages_total >> pages_rss) return pages_rss * sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE);
+  return 0;
+}
+
 void clear_model_cache() {
   std::lock_guard lock(model_cache_mutex());
-  model_cache().clear();
+  auto& cache = model_cache();
+  size_t n = cache.size();
+  if (n == 0) return;
+  size_t rss_before = get_rss_bytes();
+  cache.clear();
+  size_t rss_after = get_rss_bytes();
+  size_t freed = rss_before > rss_after ? rss_before - rss_after : 0;
+  spdlog::info(
+      "Cleared {} cached model(s), RSS {:.1f} GB -> {:.1f} GB (freed {:.1f} GB)", n,
+      rss_before / 1e9, rss_after / 1e9, freed / 1e9);
 }
 
 }  // namespace tron


<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->
---

> [!NOTE]
> **Low Risk**
> Small, localized change: a new cache-clear helper plus a test-only call site; main risk is unintended performance impact if used more broadly.
> 
> **Overview**
> Adds `tron::clear_model_cache()` to explicitly evict all entries from the global model cache.
> 
> Updates `t_generate_host_2` to clear the cache before loading the 32-layer GPTQ model, preventing previously cached 2-layer models from causing OOM in this test run.
> 
